r  proxies in the region like the houthis  against saudi arabia  and so this concept of offering the  iranians a nuclear agreement and hoping  that in return  they will somehow change their behavior  we've seen the opposite of that happen  and it's happening  as we speak while they're trying to  negotiate some kind of agreement you  know herald  critics of the president have said that  uh iran china russia  see softness so they are acting in  various different ways to challenge that  at the same time on this trip the  president has had a success in the  world's eyes at least  this vaccination effort and 500 million  vaccines that was matched just before  the show started of another 500 million  from the g7 uh take a listen to the  president  america will be the arsenal of vaccines  in our fight against global 19.  just as america was the arsenal  democracy during world war ii  our vaccine donations don't include  pressure for favors or potential consent  concessions we're doing this to save  lives  to end this pandemic that's it period we  have the lowest  number of daily deaths since the first  day of this pandemic  our economy is rebounding our  vaccination program has already saved  tens of thousands of lives obviously the  white house is touting that as a global  effort  led by the u.s harold  look that's an example of thanks for  having me on uh it's an example of our  soft power  uh this president uh was a direct attack  also i think at china a direct line of  attack at china's he said we're not  looking for concessions  or favors from uh from those nations  that we seek to help  you know i i have a little different  opinion i found i found some of the  analysis interesting  with some of the other panelists but my  perspective is slightly different i  think this effort to build  to strengthen our multilateral approach  we should say strengthen relationships  with allies build even stronger ones  with  countries we're seeking to have a better  relationship with as we enter  the the mid innings of this cold war  with china i think is a very smart thing  the world is a messy place it's a  dangerous place it always  it always has been i'm relieved a bit by  the experience this president brings and  i hope that  he and secretary blinken and secretary  austin won't be afraid to pull and use  every lever and you have to be  encouraged to hear and watch them use  the soft power lever  as as much as they are without question  the dominant organizing theme for our  foreign policy over the next five 10  15 years my kids years in middle school  and high school and college will be how  we compete and beat china that's what i  heard from the  from our military leaders today in  congress and that's what i continue to  hear  from president biden and his team as  well we should point out there was also  an attack in baghdad on the state  department compound at the airport  just last night with a drone on there  looking for the culprits there  so it's a dangerous world to your point  hey sean hannity here hey click here to  subscribe to fox news youtube page  and catch our hottest interviews and  most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else
 

